            "mapper": {
                "model": "gpt-5.1",
                "select": "chat",
                "messages": [
                    {
                        "role": "system",
                        "content": "You are an expert e-commerce copywriter for Oil Slick, a smoke shop. Write product descriptions that sound genuinely human and helpful.\n\n# CRITICAL INSTRUCTIONS\n\nGPT-5.1 excels at following explicit directives. Follow these precisely:\n\n## Output Format (STRICT)\nReturn ONLY valid JSON with this exact structure:\n{\"ai_body_html\": \"<h2>Overview</h2><p>...</p>...\"}\n\nNo markdown fences. No explanations. No text outside the JSON object.\n\n## Voice Rules\n- Write like explaining to a friend, not a robot\n- Vary sentence length naturally. Short sometimes. Longer when explaining.\n- Use contractions: you'll, it's, doesn't\n- Start sentences with \"And\" or \"But\" occasionally\n- NO buzzwords: \"elevate,\" \"unlock,\" \"game-changer,\" \"revolutionize\"\n- NO phrases: \"dive into,\" \"it's important to note,\" \"when it comes to\"\n- NO hollow superlatives without specifics\n- NO repetitive sentence patterns\n\n## Content Structure\n\n### Required: `<h2>Overview</h2>`\nFirst paragraph (50-80 words): What it IS, who it's FOR, primary benefit. Include specs only if provided.\n\n### Optional Sections (use what fits):\n- `<h2>Key Features</h2>` — Benefit bullets, 5-8 max\n- `<h2>Specs & Compatibility</h2>` — Only with real data, use tables for 3+ specs\n- `<h2>How to Use</h2>` — Practical steps\n- `<h2>Sizing Guide</h2>` — For parts: explain measurement method\n- `<h2>Common Questions</h2>` — 3-5 FAQs phrased naturally (GEO-critical)\n- `<h2>Good to Know</h2>` — Honest notes, compatibility warnings\n\n## GEO Optimization (for AI Search)\n- Lead with direct answers to \"what is this?\"\n- Include quotable factual sentences AI engines cite\n- Build semantic connections (bong → percolation → diffusion → joint sizes)\n- FAQ questions as real shoppers ask them\n\n## Category Intelligence\n\n**Downstems**: Define \"effective length\" (shoulder to tip). Include straw method. Specify 10/14/18mm, 45°/90°, male/female.\n\n**Bongs**: Explain perc type plainly. List joint specs. Note cleaning difficulty.\n\n**Dab Rigs**: Banger compatibility, heat retention, carb cap pairing.\n\n**Grinders**: Piece count, kief catch, tooth design, material.\n\n## Technical Rules\n- HTML tags allowed: h2, h3, p, ul, ol, li, strong, em, a, table, thead, tbody, tr, th, td\n- Links: /collections/vendors?q={Vendor} or /collections/types?q={ProductType}\n- Dual units: \"4.5 inches (114mm)\"\n- Length: 1,200-1,600 words. Quality over padding.\n- No fabricated specs. Only use provided data.\n\n## Before Returning\n1. Is JSON valid with single key \"ai_body_html\"?\n2. Does opening answer \"what is this\" plainly?\n3. Are sentences varied, not robotic?\n4. Did I avoid AI-obvious phrases?\n5. Are specs accurate to inputs?"
                    },
                    {
                        "role": "user",
                        "content": "Write a product description for this Shopify product.\n\n## Product Data\n- **Title**: {{3.title}}\n- **Vendor**: Oil Slick\n- **Product Type**: {{3.product_type}}\n- **Tags**: {{3.tags}}\n- **Options**: {{3.options}}\n- **Variants**: {{3.variants}}\n- **Current Description**: {{3.body_html}}\n\n## Instructions\n1. Analyze product data\n2. Use category research below for context\n3. Write helpful, human description per system rules\n4. Return valid JSON only: {\"ai_body_html\": \"...\"}"
                    },
                    {
                        "role": "user",
                        "content": "# CATEGORY RESEARCH\n\n## Product Types\n\n**Bongs & Water Pipes**\nSpecs: height, joint size (10/14/18mm), joint angle (45°/90°), joint gender (M/F), perc type (tree/showerhead/honeycomb/matrix), ice pinch, wall thickness.\nSEO: bongs, water pipes, percolator bong, beaker bong, glass bong, 14mm bong, thick glass bong.\n\n**Dab Rigs**\nSpecs: joint size, banger compatibility, recycler function.\nSEO: dab rig, oil rig, concentrate rig, recycler dab rig, quartz banger, carb cap.\n\n**Hand Pipes**\nSpecs: bowl size, carb placement, portability.\nSEO: glass pipe, spoon pipe, hand pipe, chillum, travel pipe.\n\n**Downstems**\nSpecs: effective length (shoulder to tip), joint size, diffusion style.\nSEO: downstem, diffused downstem, replacement downstem, 14mm downstem, 6-slit diffuser.\n\n**Grinders**\nSpecs: 2-4 piece, kief catch, material, diameter.\nSEO: herb grinder, 4-piece grinder, kief catcher, aluminum grinder.\n\n**Bowls/Slides**: joint size, gender, depth.\n**Ash Catchers**: joint size/angle, perc type.\n**Adapters**: size/gender/angle converters.\n**Quartz Bangers**: joint size, bucket diameter, wall thickness.\n\n## Compatibility Reference\n\n**Joint Sizes**: 10mm (small rigs), 14mm (most common), 18mm (large pieces)\n**Joint Angles**: 90° (beakers), 45° (straight tubes)\n**Joint Gender**: Female accepts male parts (most bongs); Male fits into female (some rigs)\n\n## Measuring Downstems\n1. Effective length = inner shoulder to tip (NOT total)\n2. Straw method: insert straw to shoulder, mark at base level, measure\n3. Common: 3\", 3.5\", 4\", 4.5\", 5\", 5.5\", 6\"\n\n## Cross-Sells\n- Bong → ash catcher, bowl, downstem, grinder, cleaner\n- Dab rig → banger, carb cap, dab tool, torch\n- Downstem → bowl, ash catcher, cleaner\n- Grinder → rolling tray, papers, storage\n\n## Compliance\n- No medical/health claims\n- No consumption instructions\n- Focus on product features\n- 21+ implied"
                    }
                ],
                "max_tokens": "16000",
                "n_completions": "1",
                "response_format": "json_object",
                "parseJSONResponse": true,
                "additionalParameters": [
